Reading the plate as a square dinner plate about 24 cm across, the pile of roasted sweet potato cubes covers roughly 8 cm by 7 cm in the upper right. That is about 55 cm² of footprint. The pile is about 3 cm tall, so the volume is roughly 110 to 130 cm³ once gaps between the pieces are allowed for. At about 0.8 g/cm³ for loosely packed cubes, that comes to about 100 g.

I counted about 8 to 9 pieces of roughly 3 cm each, which is consistent with that estimate. The pieces look lightly oiled, but I can't see any separate oil or sauce on the plate.

